MEAN, MEDIAN, MODE
Measures of central tendency

DATA SET x
3, 4, 6, 6, 8, 9, 10
n = 7

MEAN (average)
Formula:  x̄ = Σx / n
Σx = 3+4+6+6+8+9+10 = 46
x̄ = 46 / 7 ≈ 6.57
Uses every value. Sensitive to outliers.

MEDIAN (middle value)
Sort the data:
3  4  6  6  8  9  10
Odd n → middle position = (n+1)/2 = 4th value
Median = 6
Ignores extremes. Robust to outliers.

MODE (most frequent)
Frequency
3:1   4:1   6:2   8:1   9:1   10:1
Mode = 6
Can be none, one, or several. Useful for categorical or discrete data.

Same numbers. Three different summaries.
